## 2\. Essential Core Features

### 2.1 User Authentication and Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

* Secure registration, login, and password recovery via Supabase Auth
* Support for the following roles: Administrator, Compliance Analyst, IT/Security Team Member, Auditor, Management, and Employee/Control Owner
* Role-specific permissions governing read, write, review, approve, and admin operations
* Invitation-based team onboarding with email invitations
* Multi-organization (workspace) support with isolated data per workspace
* Session management and secure token handling

### 2.2 Compliance Dashboard

* Central overview card summarizing overall compliance score/percentage per active framework
* Visual indicators (progress rings, bar charts) for control status categories: Compliant, In Progress, Not Started, Not Applicable
* Open risks count with severity breakdown (Critical, High, Medium, Low)
* Upcoming task deadlines and overdue items highlighted
* Recent activity feed showing latest evidence uploads, task updates, and risk changes
* Quick-action shortcuts: Add Risk, Assign Task, Upload Evidence
* Notification bell for alerts, approvals pending, and deadline reminders

### 2.3 Compliance Frameworks and Controls Register

* Preloaded framework templates including:
    * ISO/IEC 27001:2022
    * SOC 2 (Trust Service Criteria)
    * NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF 2.0)
    * GDPR
    * Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 (DPDPA)
    * CERT-In Directions
    * RBI Cybersecurity Framework
* Framework selection per workspace with ability to activate multiple frameworks simultaneously
* Controls list view with filtering by domain/category, status, owner, and framework
* Individual control detail page showing: control ID, title, description, implementation guidance, linked evidence, linked risks, assigned owner, status, and audit history
* Control status management: Not Started, In Progress, Implemented, Under Review, Not Applicable
* Bulk control status updates
* Cross-framework control mapping to identify overlapping requirements

### 2.4 Risk Register

* Create, edit, and archive risk records with fields: Risk ID, Title, Description, Category, Likelihood (1–5), Impact (1–5), Inherent Risk Score (auto-calculated), Control Measures, Residual Risk Score, Risk Owner, Status (Open, Mitigating, Accepted, Closed), Due Date
* Risk matrix visualization (5x5 heatmap) filterable by category and status
* Risk-to-control linking
* Risk history/audit trail per record
* Filter and search risks by owner, category, severity, and status
* Export risk register to PDF and CSV

### 2.5 Evidence Management

* Upload documents, images, spreadsheets, and other files to a centralized evidence library
* Supported file types: PDF, DOCX, XLSX, PNG, JPG, CSV (up to 25 MB per file, stored via Supabase Storage)
* Link evidence files to one or more controls and/or audit requirements
* Evidence metadata: Title, Description, Upload Date, Uploaded By, Expiry/Review Date, Linked Controls
* Evidence status: Valid, Expiring Soon (within 30 days), Expired
* Search and filter evidence library by control, framework, status, and date
* Evidence version management (upload new version while retaining history)
* Evidence request workflow: compliance analysts can request evidence from control owners via in-app task

### 2.6 AI Compliance Assistant (Powered by OpenAI GPT-4o)

* Conversational chat interface accessible from any screen via floating action button or dedicated page
* Contextual awareness: the AI can reference the active framework, selected control, or current page context
* Capabilities:
    * Plain-language explanation of any control or regulatory requirement
    * Gap analysis suggestions based on current control statuses and missing evidence
    * Recommended next steps for remediation
    * Draft policy or procedure language suggestions
    * Summarization of uploaded evidence documents
* AI responses tagged with a disclaimer: *"AI-generated content requires review by a qualified compliance professional."*
* Chat history saved per user session and searchable
* Ability to export AI-generated suggestions as a task or note linked to a control

### 2.7 Tasks, Remediation, and Approvals

* Task creation with fields: Title, Description, Assigned To, Due Date, Priority (High/Medium/Low), Linked Control, Linked Risk, Status (Open, In Progress, Pending Review, Approved, Closed)
* Task views: My Tasks, All Tasks (admin/analyst), Overdue Tasks, Upcoming Tasks
* Approval workflow: task submitter requests review → reviewer approves or rejects with comments
* In-app notifications and email notifications for task assignments, due date reminders, and approval requests
* Task comment thread for collaboration
* Bulk task assignment and status update
* Recurring task support for periodic reviews

### 2.8 Audit Readiness and Reporting

* Audit Readiness Score displayed as a percentage per framework
* Pre-built reports:
    * Control Status Summary Report (by framework, domain, owner)
    * Evidence Coverage Report (controls with/without linked evidence)
    * Risk Summary Report (open risks by severity and category)
    * Task and Remediation Progress Report
    * Overall Compliance Health Report
* Report filters: date range, framework, control domain, owner
* Export reports to PDF and CSV
* Scheduled report generation (weekly/monthly) delivered via email
* Audit log accessible to Auditor role: read-only view of all controls, evidence, and status history

### 2.9 Notifications and Alerts

* In-app notification center with read/unread status
* Push notification support via PWA Web Push API
* Alert types: task overdue, evidence expiring, approval pending, risk escalation, new user invitation
* Notification preferences configurable per user

### 2.10 Organization/Workspace Management

* Workspace creation with organization name, industry, and logo upload
* Invite team members by email with role assignment
* View and manage all workspace members
* Deactivate or remove members
* Workspace-level settings: timezone, default framework, notification preferences

### 2.11 PWA-Specific Capabilities

* Installable on Android and iOS home screens via browser prompt
* Offline mode: cached dashboard, task list, and control list accessible without connectivity; queued actions sync on reconnect
* Responsive design optimized for mobile-first use but fully functional on tablet and desktop
* App manifest and service worker configured for full PWA compliance
* Fast-loading with lazy-loaded routes and image optimization

