## 6\. App Menu and Navigation Structure

### 6.1 Navigation System

AEGIS GRC uses a **bottom navigation bar** as the primary navigation pattern for the PWA, optimized for mobile thumb-zone accessibility. A **top app bar** provides contextual actions and branding. A **slide-out hamburger side drawer** provides access to secondary screens.

### 6.2 Bottom Navigation Bar (Persistent — All Authenticated Screens)

Five primary navigation tabs:

| Tab Icon | Label | Route |
| -------- | ----- | ----- |
| Grid / House icon | Dashboard | `/dashboard` |
| Shield / Layers icon | Frameworks | `/frameworks` |
| Alert Triangle icon | Risks | `/risks` |
| Checkbox icon | Tasks | `/tasks` |
| Sparkles / Bot icon | AI Assistant | `/ai-assistant` |

* Active tab highlighted with Electric Blue underline and icon fill
* Badge counts on Tasks tab (overdue count) and Dashboard tab (pending approvals)

### 6.3 Top App Bar

* Left: Hamburger menu icon (opens side drawer) OR back arrow on sub-screens
* Center: Page title or AEGIS GRC logo on Dashboard
* Right: Notification bell icon (with unread badge) + User avatar (opens profile/settings mini-menu)

